From 25494f4f609b126fa1eb1b820a896515df6eada5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:50:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] MiniMax-M3.1-Flash: engine loop, NCCL control link, lanes
 backend and the open() path (T8b)

engine.zig: slots over the pooled KV pages, chunked prompts that resume from adopted pages and cut at the
radix cache's marks, windows, shared windows, commit, a cancellation gate across ranks.
follow.zig: rank 0's Leader and rank 1's follow loop on the ncclBroadcast control link (the 64-byte header
of iface.zig); a lost rank ends rank 0 with RankLost, a failed follower tells the others.
backend.zig: the lanes.backend vtable (stepped prefill, copy drafts only, no vision, radix keep and restore).
draw.zig: rank 0 draws on its host from the forward's gathered fp32 logits (lane core's keyed rule, bounded heap).
engine_dev.zig: NCCL collectives, arena and block table, fingerprint byte gather, NCCL defaults (compile-checked).
engine_ops.zig is the seam to forward.zig and prefill.zig (mm3-t8a); openOps is the merge point.
native.open() joins the ranks and returns Loaded; until the merge it stops at ForwardNotBuilt.
Host tests on recording fakes: test-minimax-engine. Nothing ran on a GPU.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QguKy82jHfqdgzDsrrC5xs
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
